# Git Commits

## Commit messages

- Use **short, simple** one-line messages when possible. Example: `fix seed bcrypt hashes`, `add audit-finding-tracker sql scripts`.
- Use conventional prefixes when natural: `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `docs`, `test`, `refactor`.
- Do **not** add multi-paragraph commit bodies unless the user explicitly asks.

## Forbidden trailers and attribution

Never add any of these to commits or PRs:

- `Co-authored-by: ...` (including Cursor, Copilot, or any AI/tool)
- `Made-with: Cursor` or similar tool attribution
- Any other AI-assistant or bot co-author trailers

## Standard commit commands only

Generate plain `git` commands — no hooks, wrappers, or extras unless the user asks:

```bash
git add <paths>
git commit -m "short message here"
```

```powershell
git add <paths>
git commit -m "short message here"
```

Do **not** append trailers via `-m` body blocks, `git commit --amend` message edits, or HEREDOC bodies that include `Co-authored-by`.

Only create commits when the user explicitly requests it. Never push unless explicitly asked.
